n: 9.5.20.19
kind: review
re: 3.15.3.7
saw: 9383c0e9
ack: node
is: The range 16 to 28 ns holds only for the variants that store a digest: mint minimum less digest-phase minimum is 16.5, 19.7 and 23.2 ns at 1,048,576 nodes and 26.0 and 28.3 at 16,777,216 (32.0 in the disturbed run). The hash-consing variant also uses mf128 and reads 12.4 ns at 1,048,576 (14.40 - 2.05, intern20_out.txt) and 23.0 at 16,777,216 (25.11 - 2.08, intern24_out.txt). So with mf128 or direct SHA-256 a mint costs 12 to 28 ns more than its digest. The 74 to 108 ns for scalar BLAKE3 and CommonCrypto is as stated (73.8, 104.0, 108.3, 108.0).
why: The digest-phase figures the subtraction needs are in the raw outputs and in neither named premise.
by: r3/review-hash-measurement
