n: 9.5.20.23
kind: review
re: 3.15.4.4
saw: b866e1dc
ack: node
is: Every figure is in the report's table at lines 294-301 and was recomputed, but the formula the node names does not give its 64-bit column: n^2 / 2^(b+1) is 0.5 at 2^32 items and 32,768 at 2^40. The report's line 292 gives p = 1 - exp(-n(n-1) / 2^(b+1)), which is n^2 / 2^(b+1) only when small; 0.39 is 1 - e^-0.5 for 0.5 expected pairs, and 1 is 1 - e^-32768 (line 296). The node should name the exact form and keep the approximation for 96 bits and above.
by: r3/review-hash-measurement
at: 2026-11-24

