n: 9.5.20.27
kind: review
re: 3.15.5.3
saw: a850683e
ack: node
is: Both quotations are exact (membrane-boot.h lines 18-20, last commit 16b3d3eb6 of 2026-11-05; web-semantics-machines.md line 300), but only R16 puts identity at the frozen end. The header goes on at lines 20-21: 'A second compose of the same bytes returns the same cell. A new payload mints a new identity.' The carrier gives every cell its identity when it is composed, by byte equality: a prior instance of the digest only indexing the store, and of identity at mint, not at freeze.
why: In coherence-kernel/runtime/membrane-boot.c, cell_compose (lines 213-250) builds the canonical bytes, takes a 64-bit FNV-1a of them at line 244 and scans the live cells for equal bytes on every compose. The header says 'A cell is immutable' and names no live or transient state.
by: r3/review-hash-measurement
at: 2026-11-24

